        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "588d91bf-72a1-594f-bc80-5f5eda51b9b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hans Schlegel, Frank De Winne, Dirk Frimout\n- Organizations: ESA, NASA, ISS, Roscosmos, Belgian Air Component\n- Events: Space Shuttle missions, Expedition 21, Expedition 35\n\nFacts:\n- Hans Schlegel was born in Überlingen on 3 August 1951.\n- Frank De Winne was born in Ledeberg, Belgium, on 25 April 1961.\n- Hans Schlegel is a German physicist, an ESA astronaut, and a veteran of two NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Frank De Winne is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.\n- Frank De Winne was Belgium's second person in space after Dirk Frimout.\n- In 2009, Frank De Winne commanded ISS Expedition 21 and became the first ESA astronaut to command a space mission.\n- Expedition 35 was only the second ISS crew led by neither a NASA astronaut nor a Roscosmos cosmonaut, after Expedition 21 in 2009 under Frank De Winne's command.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "61ab325f-156c-5ed9-a797-423a3c887a46",
        "text": "Page: Hans Schlegel. Sentence: Hans Wilhelm Schlegel (Überlingen, 3 August 1951) is a German physicist, an ESA astronaut, and a veteran of two NASA Space Shuttle missions.\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: Frank, Viscount De Winne (born 25 April 1961, in Ledeberg, Belgium) is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: He is Belgium's second person in space (after Dirk Frimout).\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: He was the first ESA astronaut to command a space mission when he served as commander of ISS Expedition 21.\nPage: Expedition 35. Sentence: Expedition 35 was also only the second time an ISS crew is led by neither a NASA astronaut, nor a Roscosmos cosmonaut, after Expedition 21 in 2009, when ESA astronaut Frank De Winne was in command.",
